From 16ab1225e7eb6b84e114ba8de09335e235f980ab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mir Mohammad Sajedul Islam <mohammad.sajedul.islam@g.bracu.ac.bd>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 18:14:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ai): repair the AI tutor and limit it to the platform's
 subjects

The tutor failed on every request because both configured Groq models
(deepseek-r1-distill-llama-70b, llama-3.3-70b-versatile) have been
retired by Groq.

Backend
- Move provider logic to services/ai_tutor.py. Models come from
  AI_MODEL_DEEP / AI_MODEL_FAST (defaults openai/gpt-oss-120b and
  qwen/qwen3.6-27b); if one fails the other is tried.
- Read GROQ_API_KEY, falling back to AI_API_KEY (the README name).
- Student-safe errors: 503 when the key is missing or rejected, 429 when
  rate limited, 502 otherwise. Provider error text is only logged.
- Strip <think> blocks from reasoning models.
- Keep the tutor on topic: the system prompt limits it to Physics,
  Chemistry, Higher Math and the platform's lectures and sheets, and an
  off-topic marker is replaced by a fixed Bangla refusal.
- Require login for the tutor, cap questions at 2000 characters and
  rate-limit each user (20 questions per 5 minutes).
- Sessions are private to their owner; other people's sessions return 404.
- Case-insensitive email lookup, matching /auth/me.
- Conversation history is read from the database instead of trusting the
  browser; messages are saved only after the model answers.
- Count messages per session with one grouped query.

Frontend
- Use the shared API client; ping /health when the chat opens to wake the
  Render server, and explain long waits.
- Show specific messages for expired login, unreachable server, and
  tutor errors, with a Retry button where retrying can help.
- Rename the model buttons to Deep / Fast.

Docs and tests
- README and .env.example list GROQ_API_KEY and the model variables.
- Add backend tests with a fake provider (engine and router).
